<article class="env-lemma" id="0837">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0837">Lemma <span data-tag="0837">67.17.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. If $U$, $V$ are scheme theoretically dense open subspaces of $X$, then so is $U \cap V$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $W \to X$ be any étale morphism. Consider the map $\mathcal{O}(W) \to \mathcal{O}(W \times _ X V) \to \mathcal{O}(W \times _ X (V \cap U))$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0836" data-tag="0836">67.17.5</a> both maps are injective. Hence the composite is injective. Hence by Lemma <a href="/tag/0836" data-tag="0836">67.17.5</a> $U \cap V$ is scheme theoretically dense in $X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>